# QA replay of the newest What's New card, line by line (drafted in the release UI QA pass of 0.7.0, 2026-10-26): each
# line pointed at, then tapped. A line with a preview shows it on the map while the pointer is on it; a tour:N line
# previews nothing and its tap opens the tour at chapter N (docs/whats-new.md; DESIGN.md §4, *What's New*, *The tour*,
# "Keeping it current"). A developer build plays it with --dev-view --dev-script; how to run it, and what each still
# must show: whatsnew-lines.md beside this file. Times are in seconds.
#
# No version is named: the steps take the newest card, the build's own release. A card has up to five lines; on one with
# fewer, the steps past its last say "What's New <version> has <n> lines" in the app log and change nothing.

# A --dev-view session starts on settings of its own, as at a first start, so the tour opened by itself at chapter 1
# once the data was there. It ends first.
tour end
# Customs' artwork read once, so a preview staged there has its map at once.
map customs
wait 3
whatsnew
wait 1.5
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\card
whatsnew 1
wait 2
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\line-1
whatsnew click 1
wait 3
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\line-1-tap
tour end
wait 1
whatsnew 2
wait 2
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\line-2
whatsnew click 2
wait 3
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\line-2-tap
tour end
wait 1
whatsnew 3
wait 2
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\line-3
whatsnew click 3
wait 3
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\line-3-tap
tour end
wait 1
whatsnew 4
wait 2
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\line-4
whatsnew click 4
wait 3
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\line-4-tap
tour end
wait 1
whatsnew 5
wait 2
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\line-5
whatsnew click 5
wait 3
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\line-5-tap
tour end
wait 1.5
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\whatsnew-lines\end
exit
